===Green Party===
The [[Green Party of Aotearoa New Zealand|Green Party]] has a two-stage process to determine its party list: an initial list determined by attendees of the annual Green Party conference and then a vote and ordering by members of the party to either uphold the list or generate a different list voted on by the party. The initial list was published on 12 March 2026.<ref>{{cite news |last1=Ensor |first1=Jamie |title=Election 2026: Green Party MPs suffer big drops in draft list, Tamatha Paul ranked high as party hypes Māori candidates |url=https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/politics/election-2026-green-party-mps-suffer-big-drops-in-draft-list-tamatha-paul-ranked-high-as-party-hypes-maori-candidates/3LDIXF7JH5C2JPN7M4II6L2CO4/ |access-date=12 March 2026 |work=[[The New Zealand Herald]] |date=12 March 2026}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.greens.org.nz/candidates_2026 |title=Meet our candidates for 2026 |publisher=Green Party of Aotearoa New Zealand}}</ref>

